Operational health assessments provide an overall evaluation of Azure environments by reviewing infrastructure, security, governance, monitoring, and operational effectiveness.

Assessment criteria include:

* Service availability
* Incident trends
* Backup success
* Resource utilization
* Security posture
* Compliance status
* Cost optimization

For example, administrators perform quarterly operational assessments to verify that production systems continue meeting business expectations.

A real-life use case is enterprises using health assessments to prioritize future operational improvements.

Regular assessments strengthen cloud reliability and operational excellence.
